        "uncataloged": [
          {
            "findingId": "SP-002",
            "reason": "Genuine edge-case defect in the newly-added PEEK_PORT/PEEK_CONTROL_PORT kill loop (install.sh, new for-loop after the pre-existing ADDR_PORT block): `pid=\"$(lsof -tiTCP:\"$peek_port\" -sTCP:LISTEN || true)\"` can return multiple newline-separated PIDs (e.g. SO_REUSEPORT or transient duplicate listeners), and `kill \"$pid\"` then passes one invalid multi-line argument, which kill rejects and `2>/dev/null || true` silently swallows, leaving the port unfreed and the fallthrough LaunchAgent bootstrap racing a live listener. Golden GV3-148 catalogs the same lines only for code-duplication (NIT/code-style); no golden entry catalogs this multi-PID quoting correctness bug, so it is a genuine in-range defect the golden set does not catalog."
          }
        ]
      },
